  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Second aperture Gu is not a mortal Gu; it is a rank six Immortal Gu. Gu at rank five are mortal and Gu at rank six are immortal.",
      "chapters": [
        377
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_second_aperture_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "No matter how many mortal Gu Gu Immortals hold, that stock cannot match a single Immortal Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        460
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "against-immortal-gu",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "If a mortal Gu holds only a tiny fragment of the law of heaven and earth, an Immortal Gu holds a corner of the Great Dao.",
      "chapters": [
        564
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "against-immortal-gu",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "From rank one to five, relic Gu are green copper, red steel, white silver, yellow gold, and purple crystal relic Gu. Relic Gu are mortal Gu; that line has no rank six and above Immortal Gu form.",
      "chapters": [
        469
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "relic-gu-ceiling",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_relic_gu",
        "gu_purple_crystal_relic_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The text names rank five mortal Gu as a working category a Gu Immortal foundation can purchase or hold in bulk, still distinct from Immortal Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        566
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rank-five-stock",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Gu Immortals possess immortal essence; a bead of it can stand as unlimited primeval essence. That lets every Gu Immortal control large numbers of mortal Gu without lacking primeval essence.",
      "chapters": [
        587
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "use-under-immortal-essence",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mortal Gu are not Immortal Gu and have a limit to what they can endure; activating them without rest collapses them. When mortal Gu Masters use mortal Gu, primeval essence limits hide that flaw. When Gu Immortals activate mortal Gu, the endurance issue becomes conspicuous.",
      "chapters": [
        642
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "use-under-immortal-essence",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Gu at rank six and above are covered on Immortal Gu. Gu as living tools are covered on Gu worms.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "use-under-immortal-essence",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_immortal_gu",
        "sys_gu_worms"
      ]
    }
  ],
